[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, y=0.35cm]
\fill[gray!35] (2,0) -- (2,4) -- (5,13) -- (5,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-1.2,0) -- (6.2,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-4) -- (0,17) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,<->] (-0.3,-2.9) -- (5.5,14.5);
\node at (3.4,12) {$y=3x-2$};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4,5} \draw (\x,0.5) -- (\x,-0.5) node[below,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$\x$};
\foreach \y in {4,8,12} \draw (0.1,\y) -- (-0.1,\y) node[left,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$\y$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Which definite integral gives the area of the shaded region?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\fill[gray!35] (-1,0) -- (-1,1.4) -- plot[smooth,domain=-1:5,variable=\x] ({\x},{0.2*\x*\x+1.2}) -- (5,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-2.6,0) -- (6,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-0.8) -- (0,7.8) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,<->,domain=-2:5.4,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{0.2*\x*\x+1.2});
\node at (-1.4,5.6) {$y=f(x)$};
\foreach \x in {-0.5,0,0.5,1,1.5,2,2.5,3,3.5,4,4.5} \draw[dashed] (\x,0) -- (\x,{0.2*\x*\x+1.2});
\draw (-1,0.15) -- (-1,-0.15) node[below,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$-1$};
\draw (5,0.15) -- (5,-0.15) node[below,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$5$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The interval $-1\le x\le 5$ is divided into $12$ equal strips. What is $\Delta x$?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\fill[gray!35] (0,0.8) -- plot[smooth,domain=0:5,variable=\x] ({\x},{0.15*\x*\x+0.8}) -- (5,0) -- (0,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-0.6,0) -- (6.2,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-0.8) -- (0,6.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,->,domain=0:5.6,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{0.15*\x*\x+0.8});
\node at (1.2,4.4) {$y=f(x)$};
\foreach \x in {0.5,1,1.5,2,2.5,3,3.5,4,4.5} \draw[dashed] (\x,0) -- (\x,{0.15*\x*\x+0.8});
\draw (5,0.15) -- (5,-0.15) node[below] {$5$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The interval $0\le x\le 5$ is divided into $10$ equal strips, as shown. How many boundary points $x_{0},x_{1},x_{2},\dots$ are there?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=0.6cm, y=0.25cm]
\fill[gray!35] (3,0) -- (3,11) -- (8,21) -- (8,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-1.2,0) -- (10.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-3) -- (0,26) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,<->] (-0.5,4) -- (9.6,24.2);
\node at (2,18) {$y=2x+5$};
\foreach \x in {2,4,6,8} \draw (\x,0.7) -- (\x,-0.7) node[below,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$\x$};
\foreach \y in {5,10,15,20} \draw (0.15,\y) -- (-0.15,\y) node[left,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$\y$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The shaded area is estimated by rectangles of width $\Delta x$. Which definite integral does $\lim_{\Delta x\to 0}\sum_{3}^{8}(2x+5)\,\Delta x$ equal?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, y=0.4cm]
\fill[gray!35] (0,0) -- (0,-9) -- plot[smooth,domain=0:2,variable=\x] ({\x},{\x*\x-9}) -- (2,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-4,0) -- (4.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-11) -- (0,4.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,<->,domain=-3.4:3.4,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{\x*\x-9});
\node at (2.6,-6) {$y=x^{2}-9$};
\foreach \x in {-3,-2,-1,1,2,3} \draw (\x,0.4) -- (\x,-0.4) node[below,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$\x$};
\foreach \y in {-9,-6,-3,3} \draw (0.1,\y) -- (-0.1,\y) node[left,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$\y$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Which statement about $\int_{0}^{2}(x^{2}-9)\,dx$ is correct?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=0.28cm, y=0.5cm]
\fill[gray!35] (0,0) -- (0,2) -- (20,8) -- (20,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-3,0) -- (25,0) node[right] {$t$ (s)};
\draw[->] (0,-1.5) -- (0,10.5) node[above] {$R$ (kg/s)};
\draw[thick,->] (-2,1.4) -- (23,8.9);
\node at (6,8) {$R=0.3t+2$};
\foreach \x in {5,10,15,20} \draw (\x,0.2) -- (\x,-0.2) node[below] {$\x$};
\foreach \y in {2,4,6,8} \draw (0.4,\y) -- (-0.4,\y) node[left] {$\y$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Grain falls onto a pile at a rate $R$ kilograms per second over $0\le t\le 20$ seconds. What does $\sum_{0}^{20}R\,\Delta t$ estimate?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, y=0.5cm]
\fill[gray!35] (-4,0) -- (-4,2) -- (1,7) -- (1,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-7.4,0) -- (3.2,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-1.8) -- (0,9.6) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,<->] (-6.5,-0.5) -- (2,8);
\node at (-4.6,6.5) {$y=x+6$};
\foreach \x in {-6,-4,-2,2} \draw (\x,0.2) -- (\x,-0.2) node[below,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$\x$};
\foreach \y in {2,4,6,8} \draw (0.1,\y) -- (-0.1,\y) node[left,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$\y$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The shaded region is measured by $\int_{-4}^{1}(x+6)\,dx$. Which statement about this integral is correct?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=0.5cm, y=0.35cm]
\fill[gray!35] (2,0) -- (2,10) -- plot[smooth,domain=2:10,variable=\x] ({\x},{20/\x}) -- (10,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-1.6,0) -- (13.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-2) -- (0,16.5) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,<->,domain=1.4:12,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{20/\x});
\node at (7,9) {$y=\frac{20}{x}$};
\foreach \x in {2,4,6,8,10} \draw (\x,0.4) -- (\x,-0.4) node[below] {$\x$};
\foreach \y in {4,8,12} \draw (0.2,\y) -- (-0.2,\y) node[left] {$\y$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The shaded region is split into $n$ equal strips of width $\Delta x$, and each rectangle's height is read from a point in its own strip. Which expression gives the exact area of the region?
